              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: Out-of-bounds read and write while processing binary containing reloc(s) with negative addresses"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Binary File Descriptor (BFD) library (aka libbfd), as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.28, is vulnerable to an invalid read of size 1 and an invalid write of size 1 during processing of a corrupt binary containing reloc(s) with negative addresses. This vulnerability causes programs that conduct an analysis of binary programs using the libbfd library, such as objdump, to crash."
