              "id": "CVE-2018-5710",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "krb5: null pointer deference in strlen function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) through 1.16. The pre-defined function \"strlen\" is getting a \"NULL\" string as a parameter value in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c in the Key Distribution Center (KDC), which allows remote authenticated users to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference) via a modified kadmin client."
              },
