              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It was discovered systemd does not correctly check the content of PIDFile files before using it to kill processes. When a service is run from an unprivileged user (e.g. User field set in the service file), a local attacker who is able to write to the PIDFile of the mentioned service may use this flaw to trick systemd into killing other services and/or privileged processes. Versions before v237 are vulnerable."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-16888",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2018-16888\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: udev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2018-16888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-16888)\nIt was discovered systemd does not correctly check the content of PIDFile files before using it to kill processes. When a service is run from an unprivileged user (e.g. User field set in the service file), a local attacker who is able to write to the PIDFile of the mentioned service may use this flaw to trick systemd into killing other services and/or privileged processes. Versions before v237 are vulnerable.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2018-16888**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|udev||[CVE-2018-16888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-16888)|\n\nIt was discovered systemd does not correctly check the content of PIDFile files before using it to kill processes. When a service is run from an unprivileged user (e.g. User field set in the service file), a local attacker who is able to write to the PIDFile of the mentioned service may use this flaw to trick systemd into killing other services and/or privileged processes. Versions before v237 are vulnerable."
              },
