            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-3815",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "systemd: memory leak in journald-server.c introduced by fix for CVE-2018-16864"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A memory leak was discovered in the backport of fixes for CVE-2018-16864 in Red Hat Enterprise Linux. Function dispatch_message_real() in journald-server.c does not free the memory allocated by set_iovec_field_free() to store the `_CMDLINE=` entry. A local attacker may use this flaw to make systemd-journald crash. This issue only affects versions shipped with Red Hat Enterprise since v219-62.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-3815",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-3815\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: udev\nFixed Version: 215-17+deb8u11\nLink: [CVE-2019-3815](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-3815)\nA memory leak was discovered in the backport of fixes for CVE-2018-16864 in Red Hat Enterprise Linux. Function dispatch_message_real() in journald-server.c does not free the memory allocated by set_iovec_field_free() to store the `_CMDLINE=` entry. A local attacker may use this flaw to make systemd-journald crash. This issue only affects versions shipped with Red Hat Enterprise since v219-62.2.",
