            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-3900",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Kernel: vhost_net: infinite loop while receiving packets leads to DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An infinite loop issue was found in the vhost_net kernel module in Linux Kernel up to and including v5.1-rc6, while handling incoming packets in handle_rx(). It could occur if one end sends packets faster than the other end can process them. A guest user, maybe remote one, could use this flaw to stall the vhost_net kernel thread, resulting in a DoS scenario."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-3900",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-3900\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.72-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-3900](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-3900)\nAn infinite loop issue was found in the vhost_net kernel module in Linux Kernel up to and including v5.1-rc6, while handling incoming packets in handle_rx(). It could occur if one end sends packets faster than the other end can process them. A guest user, maybe remote one, could use this flaw to stall the vhost_net kernel thread, resulting in a DoS scenario.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-3900**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev|3.16.72-1|[CVE-2019-3900](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-3900)|\n\nAn infinite loop issue was found in the vhost_net kernel module in Linux Kernel up to and including v5.1-rc6, while handling incoming packets in handle_rx(). It could occur if one end sends packets faster than the other end can process them. A guest user, maybe remote one, could use this flaw to stall the vhost_net kernel thread, resulting in a DoS scenario."
              },
