            {
              "id": "CVE-2016-10741",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: race condition between direct and memory-mapped I/O in fs/xfs/xfs_aops.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel before 4.9.3, fs/xfs/xfs_aops.c allows local users to cause a denial of service (system crash) because there is a race condition between direct and memory-mapped I/O (associated with a hole) that is handled with BUG_ON instead of an I/O failure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
