              "id": "CVE-2018-19985",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: oob memory read in hso_probe in drivers/net/usb/hso.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The function hso_get_config_data in drivers/net/usb/hso.c in the Linux kernel through 4.19.8 reads if_num from the USB device (as a u8) and uses it to index a small array, resulting in an object out-of-bounds (OOB) read that potentially allows arbitrary read in the kernel address space."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-19985",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2018-19985\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.64-1\nLink: [CVE-2018-19985](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-19985)\nThe function hso_get_config_data in drivers/net/usb/hso.c in the Linux kernel through 4.19.8 reads if_num from the USB device (as a u8) and uses it to index a small array, resulting in an object out-of-bounds (OOB) read that potentially allows arbitrary read in the kernel address space.",
