            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-11190",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ASLR bypass for setuid binaries due to late install_exec_creds()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Linux kernel before 4.8 allows local users to bypass ASLR on setuid programs (such as /bin/su) because install_exec_creds() is called too late in load_elf_binary() in fs/binfmt_elf.c, and thus the ptrace_may_access() check has a race condition when reading /proc/pid/stat."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-11190",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-11190\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.68-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-11190](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-11190)\nThe Linux kernel before 4.8 allows local users to bypass ASLR on setuid programs (such as /bin/su) because install_exec_creds() is called too late in load_elf_binary() in fs/binfmt_elf.c, and thus the ptrace_may_access() check has a race condition when reading /proc/pid/stat.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-11190**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.68-1|[CVE-2019-11190](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-11190)|\n\nThe Linux kernel before 4.8 allows local users to bypass ASLR on setuid programs (such as /bin/su) because install_exec_creds() is called too late in load_elf_binary() in fs/binfmt_elf.c, and thus the ptrace_may_access() check has a race condition when reading /proc/pid/stat."
              },
              "properties": {
