            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-14283",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: integer overflow and OOB read in drivers/block/floppy.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, set_geometry in drivers/block/floppy.c does not validate the sect and head fields, as demonstrated by an integer overflow and out-of-bounds read. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user when a floppy disk has been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14283",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-14283\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.72-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-14283](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14283)\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, set_geometry in drivers/block/floppy.c does not validate the sect and head fields, as demonstrated by an integer overflow and out-of-bounds read. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user when a floppy disk has been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-14283**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.72-1|[CVE-2019-14283](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14283)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, set_geometry in drivers/block/floppy.c does not validate the sect and head fields, as demonstrated by an integer overflow and out-of-bounds read. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user when a floppy disk has been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv2_score": 4.6,
