            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-14284",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: denial of service in drivers/block/floppy.c by setup_format_params division-by-zero"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, drivers/block/floppy.c allows a denial of service by setup_format_params division-by-zero. Two consecutive ioctls can trigger the bug: the first one should set the drive geometry with .sect and .rate values that make F_SECT_PER_TRACK be zero. Next, the floppy format operation should be called. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user even when a floppy disk has not been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14284",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-14284\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.72-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-14284](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14284)\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, drivers/block/floppy.c allows a denial of service by setup_format_params division-by-zero. Two consecutive ioctls can trigger the bug: the first one should set the drive geometry with .sect and .rate values that make F_SECT_PER_TRACK be zero. Next, the floppy format operation should be called. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user even when a floppy disk has not been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-14284**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.72-1|[CVE-2019-14284](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14284)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2.3, drivers/block/floppy.c allows a denial of service by setup_format_params division-by-zero. Two consecutive ioctls can trigger the bug: the first one should set the drive geometry with .sect and .rate values that make F_SECT_PER_TRACK be zero. Next, the floppy format operation should be called. It can be triggered by an unprivileged local user even when a floppy disk has not been inserted. NOTE: QEMU creates the floppy device by default."
              },
