            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-19227",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: potential NULL pointer dereference leads to DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the AppleTalk subsystem in the Linux kernel before 5.1, there is a potential NULL pointer dereference because register_snap_client may return NULL. This will lead to denial of service in net/appletalk/aarp.c and net/appletalk/ddp.c, as demonstrated by unregister_snap_client, aka CID-9804501fa122."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19227",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-19227\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.81-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-19227](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19227)\nIn the AppleTalk subsystem in the Linux kernel before 5.1, there is a potential NULL pointer dereference because register_snap_client may return NULL. This will lead to denial of service in net/appletalk/aarp.c and net/appletalk/ddp.c, as demonstrated by unregister_snap_client, aka CID-9804501fa122.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-19227**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.81-1|[CVE-2019-19227](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19227)|\n\nIn the AppleTalk subsystem in the Linux kernel before 5.1, there is a potential NULL pointer dereference because register_snap_client may return NULL. This will lead to denial of service in net/appletalk/aarp.c and net/appletalk/ddp.c, as demonstrated by unregister_snap_client, aka CID-9804501fa122."
