            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-19319",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: out-of-bounds write in ext4_xattr_set_entry in fs/ext4/xattr.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel before 5.2, a setxattr operation, after a mount of a crafted ext4 image, can cause a slab-out-of-bounds write access because of an ext4_xattr_set_entry use-after-free in fs/ext4/xattr.c when a large old_size value is used in a memset call, aka CID-345c0dbf3a30."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19319",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-19319\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.84-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-19319](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19319)\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2, a setxattr operation, after a mount of a crafted ext4 image, can cause a slab-out-of-bounds write access because of an ext4_xattr_set_entry use-after-free in fs/ext4/xattr.c when a large old_size value is used in a memset call, aka CID-345c0dbf3a30.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-19319**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.84-1|[CVE-2019-19319](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19319)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel before 5.2, a setxattr operation, after a mount of a crafted ext4 image, can cause a slab-out-of-bounds write access because of an ext4_xattr_set_entry use-after-free in fs/ext4/xattr.c when a large old_size value is used in a memset call, aka CID-345c0dbf3a30."
