            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-19332",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Kernel: kvm: OOB memory write via kvm_dev_ioctl_get_cpuid"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An out-of-bounds memory write issue was found in the Linux Kernel, version 3.13 through 5.4, in the way the Linux kernel's KVM hypervisor handled the 'KVM_GET_EMULATED_CPUID' ioctl(2) request to get CPUID features emulated by the KVM hypervisor. A user or process able to access the '/dev/kvm' device could use this flaw to crash the system, resulting in a denial of service."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19332",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-19332\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 3.16.81-1\nLink: [CVE-2019-19332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19332)\nAn out-of-bounds memory write issue was found in the Linux Kernel, version 3.13 through 5.4, in the way the Linux kernel's KVM hypervisor handled the 'KVM_GET_EMULATED_CPUID' ioctl(2) request to get CPUID features emulated by the KVM hypervisor. A user or process able to access the '/dev/kvm' device could use this flaw to crash the system, resulting in a denial of service.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-19332**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|3.16.81-1|[CVE-2019-19332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-19332)|\n\nAn out-of-bounds memory write issue was found in the Linux Kernel, version 3.13 through 5.4, in the way the Linux kernel's KVM hypervisor handled the 'KVM_GET_EMULATED_CPUID' ioctl(2) request to get CPUID features emulated by the KVM hypervisor. A user or process able to access the '/dev/kvm' device could use this flaw to crash the system, resulting in a denial of service."
              },
