            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-10769",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Buffer over-read in crypto_authenc_extractkeys() when a payload longer than 4 bytes is not aligned."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A buffer over-read flaw was found in RH kernel versions before 5.0 in crypto_authenc_extractkeys in crypto/authenc.c in the IPsec Cryptographic algorithm's module, authenc. When a payload longer than 4 bytes, and is not following 4-byte alignment boundary guidelines, it causes a buffer over-read threat, leading to a system crash. This flaw allows a local attacker with user privileges to cause a denial of service."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2020-10769",
