            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-11884",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: sensitive information disclosure from kernel stack memory via HIDPCONNADD command"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The do_hidp_sock_ioctl function in net/bluetooth/hidp/sock.c in the Linux kernel before 5.0.15 allows a local user to obtain potentially sensitive information from kernel stack memory via a HIDPCONNADD command, because a name field may not end with a '\\0' character."
