            {
              "id": "CVE-2015-6563",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "openssh: Privilege separation weakness related to PAM support"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The monitor component in sshd in OpenSSH before 7.0 on non-OpenBSD platforms accepts extraneous username data in MONITOR_REQ_PAM_INIT_CTX requests, which allows local users to conduct impersonation attacks by leveraging any SSH login access in conjunction with control of the sshd uid to send a crafted MONITOR_REQ_PWNAM request, related to monitor.c and monitor_wrap.c."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2015-6563",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2015-6563\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: openssh-client\nFixed Version: 1:6.7p1-5+deb8u6\nLink: [CVE-2015-6563](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2015-6563)\nThe monitor component in sshd in OpenSSH before 7.0 on non-OpenBSD platforms accepts extraneous username data in MONITOR_REQ_PAM_INIT_CTX requests, which allows local users to conduct impersonation attacks by leveraging any SSH login access in conjunction with control of the sshd uid to send a crafted MONITOR_REQ_PWNAM request, related to monitor.c and monitor_wrap.c.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2015-6563**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|openssh-client|1:6.7p1-5+deb8u6|[CVE-2015-6563](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2015-6563)|\n\nThe monitor component in sshd in OpenSSH before 7.0 on non-OpenBSD platforms accepts extraneous username data in MONITOR_REQ_PAM_INIT_CTX requests, which allows local users to conduct impersonation attacks by leveraging any SSH login access in conjunction with control of the sshd uid to send a crafted MONITOR_REQ_PWNAM request, related to monitor.c and monitor_wrap.c."
