            {
              "id": "GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Global node_modules Binary Overwrite in bin-links"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Versions of  `bin-links` prior to 1.1.6 are vulnerable to a Global node_modules Binary Overwrite. It fails to prevent globally-installed binaries to be overwritten by other package installs. For example, if a package was installed globally and created a `serve` binary, any subsequent installs of packages that also create a `serve` binary would overwrite the first binary. This behavior is still allowed in local installations.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.6 or later."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: bin-links\nFixed Version: 1.1.6\nLink: [GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98)\nVersions of  `bin-links` prior to 1.1.6 are vulnerable to a Global node_modules Binary Overwrite. It fails to prevent globally-installed binaries to be overwritten by other package installs. For example, if a package was installed globally and created a `serve` binary, any subsequent installs of packages that also create a `serve` binary would overwrite the first binary. This behavior is still allowed in local installations.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.6 or later.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|bin-links|1.1.6|[GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v45m-2wcp-gg98)|\n\nVersions of  `bin-links` prior to 1.1.6 are vulnerable to a Global node_modules Binary Overwrite. It fails to prevent globally-installed binaries to be overwritten by other package installs. For example, if a package was installed globally and created a `serve` binary, any subsequent installs of packages that also create a `serve` binary would overwrite the first binary. This behavior is still allowed in local installations.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to version 1.1.6 or later."
